We need to build complete route JSON. We have target molecule? The apply_template gave precursors list: ["CC(=C(c1ccccc1))CCCC(=O)C(F)(F)F"] That's a single precursor? The template likely is a reaction that forms product from that precursor plus something else? The mapped_rxn shows transformation: left side: ([CH3:1]/[C:2]([c:3]1... )=[CH:9]/[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C:13](=[O:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18]) >> right side product with OH etc. So left side includes a chain with carbonyl and CF3, plus a double bond to aromatic etc. The product adds OH to carbonyl carbon? Actually left side has C=O? left side: ...[C:13](=[O:14])[C:15]... right side: ...[C@@:13]1([OH:14])... So left side carbonyl becomes alcohol? So reaction is reduction of ketone to alcohol? The precursor list only includes one molecule, but reaction likely also needs a reducing agent (e.g., NaBH4). But in retrosynthesis, the precursor is the ketone, and the other reactant is a reducing agent (maybe H2). The route likely includes that reaction with template_id 1914384. So we need JSON: root molecule is target product (the product SMILES). We need its SMILES. Not given directly. We have precursor SMILES: "CC(=C(c1ccccc1))CCCC(=O)C(F)(F)F". That's the ketone. The product is the reduced alcohol: need to get SMILES from mapped_rxn product side. The mapped_rxn product side: "([CH3:1][C@H:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)[C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([OH:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18])". Remove atom mapping and stereochemistry? Let's convert to SMILES: CH3 attached to chiral carbon with aromatic ring etc. Probably product SMILES: "CC(Cc1ccccc1)CCCC(C(F)(F)F)O"? Wait need to reconstruct.

Let's decode: CH3 attached to C@H (center) which is attached to aromatic ring (c1ccccc1) and also attached to C@@H (position 9) which is part of a cyclobutane? Actually [C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([OH:14])... So a cyclobutane ring (4-member) with OH on carbon 13 and attached to CF3 carbon (C:15). So product is a bicyclic? Actually it's a cyclobutane fused? Hard.

Maybe easier: The product SMILES can be derived by applying reduction to the ketone: the ketone carbonyl becomes alcohol. So product SMILES: "CC(=C(c1ccccc1))CCCC(C(F)(F)F)O". That seems plausible: original precursor: "CC(=C(c1ccccc1))CCCC(=O)C(F)(F)F". Replace (=O) with O (alcohol). So product SMILES: "CC(=C(c1ccccc1))CCCC(C(F)(F)F)O". Let's use that.

Now need route JSON: root mol with product SMILES, children reaction node with template_id 1914384, children list of precursor mol(s). The reaction likely also includes a reducing agent, but not given. We'll include only the ketone precursor. Could also include "H2" as second reactant? Not provided. We'll just include the precursor.

Thus JSON:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"CC(=C(c1ccccc1))CCCC(C(F)(F)F)O",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":1914384,
     "children":[
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"CC(=C(c1ccccc1))CCCC(=O)C(F)(F)F"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

We should verify route schema using verify_route tool.
